// probe_spells.hml — acceptance probe for src/sim/spells.hml (the spell school).
//
// Run it FROM THE NIGHTSHADE REPO ROOT, both ways:
//     hemlockc -O1 tools/probe_spells.hml -o /tmp/pspell && /tmp/pspell
//     hemlock  tools/probe_spells.hml
//
// It exits 1 on any failure AND on an assertion-count mismatch.  It links no
// SDL: `nm /tmp/pspell | grep -c SDL_` must print 0.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT THIS PROBE ASSERTS, AND WHAT IT REFUSES TO
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CLAUDE.md rule 5: "assert the design, not the digits — but pin design ANCHORS
// with a literal."  So the literals below are exactly the ones that ARE the
// design, written in DIRECTION.md and MAGIC_KINETIC.md in a programmer's own
// numbers, and nothing else:
//
//     the owner's three verbs exist        healing, fire blasts, cloaking
//     the fire blast is the Emberlance     60 impact + 12/s burn, 3.5 m AoE
//     the fire blast is KINETIC            §1.1 — a spell is a DELIVERY kind
//     the cloak has a TELL                 6 m, and the lantern never goes out
//     Attunement moves three numbers       slots, potency, cooldown  (§9)
//     nothing magic reaches past 24 m      §1.3
//     no multiplier is ever below 0.15     §5.3 THE LAW
//
// Everything else is asserted as a RELATIONSHIP: cost falls monotonically with
// Attunement, damage falls monotonically with distance, the beam bills at 10 Hz
// no matter how fast the caller casts, oil regen is exact over a whole minute,
// the state round-trips, the hash separates.  Those survive a retune; a table
// of frozen digits does not, and this project has already been burned twice by
// probes that encoded consequences as constants.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE ONE THING IT CANNOT TEST
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// `spells.hml` is NOT WIRED INTO `sim.hml`'s tick order — that file is not
// owned by this task and the tick order is API (CLAUDE.md §7).  So this probe
// drives `spell_step` and `spell_cast` directly.  Every number below is real
// and measured; none of it is reachable from a keypress yet.  Said plainly in
// the task report rather than buried here.

